      "url": "https://github.com/mugmarp/sams-attendance/pull/1",
      "title": "Complete SAMS attendance prototype with verified role and offline workflows",
      "body": "Complete the unfinished SAMS prototype so a lecturer can open a dated class, an enrolled student can check in with its current code, and the registrar can review a correct attendance report. Preserve the original Hermes work in history and keep the existing React/Express/PostgreSQL stack.\n\nThe backend now owns check-in state transactionally in PostgreSQL, enforces role/enrollment/ownership rules, handles retries without duplicate attendance, and records reasoned lecturer corrections. Reports count completed classes in the selected course offering, handle zero-session cases, and distinguish attendance qualification from final examination clearance. Demo seeding and validated local imports replace silent mismatched timetable loading.\n\nThe frontend completes the three role journeys, updates codes/rosters, provides working report filters and PDF downloads, and supports a cached app shell plus user-scoped pending/failed offline attempts. Offline attempts are accepted only when the server validates the current code; device timestamps cannot backdate attendance.\n\nValidation: both applications build and pass strict TypeScript checks; 15 backend/API/import tests and 3 browser journeys pass locally against isolated PostgreSQL. Demo seeding is repeatable, the import CLI succeeds, dependency audits are clean, and all pages of a populated multi-page PDF were rendered and inspected. GitHub CI passed all checks, both container image builds, and a full Compose smoke deployment covering migrations, runtime demo seeding, health, login and safe authenticated nginx proxy responses. Local Docker execution was unavailable, so those deployment checks ran on the hosted runner.\n\nDeployment instructions, environment examples, committed migrations, API documentation, a Postman collection, implementation plan and verification record are included. This remains a classroom prototype: no official MUST approval, SSO, fee/coursework clearance, production account lifecycle, public deployment or migration of real student records is claimed. Review the documented boundaries before using institutional data.\n\nHosted verification: https://github.com/mugmarp/sams-attendance/actions/runs/43026546708 (success).\n",
