    {
      "number": 2,
      "url": "https://github.com/mugmarp/sams-attendance/pull/2",
      "title": "Deliver JavaScript SAMS with offline attendance, academic structure and account controls",
      "body": "SAMS now runs as plain HTML/CSS/JavaScript served by Express with PostgreSQL, with attendance, academic filtering, timetable review, offline register synchronization and account recovery.\n\nProgramme course plans connect student registrations to the current academic term and approved compulsory/elective offerings. Students receive missing compulsory links on sign-in or workspace entry and confirm electives in My courses. Registrar preview/publish and cohort assignment preserve withdrawals and existing dates. Programme-specific offering keys keep reused course codes distinct. Report dates explicitly convert stored UTC instants to Kampala dates.\n\nValidation: 61 backend tests, 34 browser tests, 135 Postman requests and 351 assertions passed. GitHub checks passed for the feature and provisioning fix. Native release cbcc946 is deployed with 13 pilot plans covering 53 students. Existing manual enrollments, sessions and marks were preserved; a fresh recovery dump restored and its downloaded copy passed checksum verification. Testing history and sanitized totals are indexed in docs/TESTING_HISTORY.md.\n\nPilot lecturer accounts and compulsory classifications are project data requiring institutional review. Ambiguous source labels are excluded. Dated classes remain a lecturer/timetable review action. Remaining audit findings concerning privileged account creation, scheduling conflicts, offering validation and long-title PDFs are still open. Physical Android acceptance and measured workload capacity are not claimed.\n",
